  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, avatar culling is performed based on the download size and uncompressed size, but even with a download size of around 50MB, avatars that would have a significant negative impact on the actual frame rate, such as\n\nmore than 1,000,000 polygons\n\nmore than 100 Physbone components\n\n500MB of texture memory\n\nwill not be culled.\n\nTherefore, I would like to see a feature added to cull based on polygon count, number of Physbone components, and texture memory size.\n\nAlso, when culling based on Physbone component count, I would like a setting that disables physics calculations only, rather than imposter display, like in the old days when DynamicBone was used.",
